7-Day Study Plan (July 11 – July 17)

Given your existing experience with PySpark, AWS Glue, Lambda orchestration, and Lake Formation, you have a strong foundation. Here's an optimized plan:

Day 1 (July 11) – Domain 1: Data Ingestion (Part 1)

    Kinesis Data Streams vs. Firehose vs. Analytics — when to use which
    AWS DMS — full load vs. CDC, source/target configurations
    AppFlow for SaaS integrations
    Batch vs. real-time ingestion patterns
    Practice: 15 questions on ingestion

Day 2 (July 12) – Domain 1: Data Transformation (Part 2)

    AWS Glue deep dive — Job Bookmarks, Crawlers, DynamicFrames vs. DataFrames
    Spark on EMR — cluster sizing, EMRFS, transient vs. persistent clusters
    Data formats: Parquet vs. ORC vs. Avro (when to use each)
    Schema evolution and schema registry
    Practice: 15 questions on transformation

Day 3 (July 13) – Domain 2: Data Store Management (Part 1)

    S3 — storage classes, lifecycle policies, versioning, replication
    Redshift — distribution styles, sort keys, COPY command, Spectrum, concurrency scaling
    Data modeling — star schema, denormalization for analytics
    Practice: 15 questions on data stores

Day 4 (July 14) – Domain 2: Data Store Management (Part 2)

    DynamoDB — partition keys, GSI/LSI, streams, capacity modes
    RDS/Aurora — read replicas, Multi-AZ, Aurora Serverless
    Lake Formation — blueprints, governed tables, tag-based access
    Data lake architecture patterns (raw → curated → consumption)
    Practice: 15 questions on data stores

Day 5 (July 15) – Domain 3: Data Operations & Support

    MWAA (Managed Airflow) — DAGs, scheduling, sensors
    Step Functions — orchestrating Glue/Lambda/EMR workflows
    EventBridge — event-driven pipelines
    CloudWatch — metrics, alarms, Logs Insights for pipeline debugging
    Data quality — Glue Data Quality, Great Expectations patterns
    Practice: 15 questions on operations

Day 6 (July 16) – Domain 4: Data Security & Governance

    IAM policies for data services (S3, Glue, Redshift)
    Lake Formation fine-grained access (row/column-level security)
